'''Entity [[Tag_(Java_Edition)|tags]]'''
* Added {{cd|#cannot_be_age_locked}}
** Defines which baby mobs that age that can not have its aging stopped using a [[golden dandelion]].

'''[[Environment attribute]]s'''
* {{cd|minecraft:visual/block_light_tint}}
** Tint of the block light. Block light color start as dark grey at low light levels, becomes tinted by this attribute at medium levels and turns white at high levels. By default, it provides the yellowish tint of torches. Bright colors work best for this attribute, with at least one color component being fully bright. The tint applies globally to all light sources visible on the screen. Individual lights can not be tinted differently.
** Value type: RGB color
** Default value: {{color|#FFD88C}}
** Modifiers: RGB Color Modifiers
** Interpolated: yes
** Resolved at the camera's position

* {{cd|minecraft:visual/ambient_light_color}}
** Defines both the ambient light tint and brightness. This light is applied to the world at 0 light level. Block and sky light are added on top of it.
** Value type: RGB color
** Default value: {{color|#000000}}.
** Modifiers: RGB Color Modifiers
** Interpolated: yes
** Resolved at the camera's position.
** Set to {{color|#0A0A0A}} in the Overworld, {{color|#302821}} in the Nether, and {{color|#3f473f}} in the End.

* {{cd|minecraft:visual/night_vision_color}}
** This color is used similarly to ambient light color. When the Night Vision effect is active, per-component maximum of {{cd|minecraft:visual/night_vision_color}} and {{cd|minecraft:visual/ambient_light_color}} is used as ambient color. [[Night Vision]] is not tinted by default.
** Value type: RGB color
** Default value: {{color|#999999}}
** Modifiers: RGB Color Modifiers
** Interpolated: yes
** Resolved at the camera's position

'''Fluid [[Tag_(Java_Edition)|tags]]'''
* Added tags to determine which fluids can support the following blocks:
** {{cd|#supports_lily_pad}}
** {{cd|#supports_frogspawn}}
* Added {{cd|#supports_sugar_cane_adjacently}}
** Contains fluids satisfy adjacency support requirements for [[sugar cane]].
* Added {{cd|#bubble_columns_can_occupy}} fluid tag to define which fluids a [[bubble column]] can occupy with water as default.

'''Item [[Tag_(Java_Edition)|tags]]'''
* Added {{cd|#metal_nuggets}}
** Contains all types of [[nugget]]s.
* Added {{cd|#dyes}}
** Contains all vanilla [[dye]]s.
* Added {{cd|#loom_dyes}}
** Contains all items that are allowed in the Loom screen to set pattern colors.
** The [[loom]] screen also requires the minecraft:dye component to be present on item stacks.
* Added {{cd|#loom_patterns}}
** Contains all items that are allowed in the loom screen to unlock patterns.
** The loom screen also requires the {{cd|minecraft:provides_banner_patterns}} component to be present on item stacks.
* Add

